V: Kenyan Primary School Management System (SaaS Architecture Blueprint)
Enterprise UI Architecture, RBAC, and Navigation Blueprint

1. Gateway & Authentication Module
----------------------------------

Page 1.1: Multi-Tenant Login Portal
- Viewport Priority: Mobile-First (Responsive Layout).
- UI Components:
  • Dynamic School Branding Header (loads custom logo based on sub-domain context, e.g., nairobiacademy.skulapp.ke).
  • Form input fields: Tenant Identification ID/School Code, Email Address / Admission Number, and Password Secure Field.
  • Visibility Toggle icon (reveal password strings).
  • CTA Primary Button: Sign In.
- UI Workflow Actions:
  1. System inspects the entered Tenant ID via an API lookahead check to ensure the school account is active.
  2. User submits login forms. If successful, the API returns a JWT containing metadata for the user's explicit authorization role mapping.
  3. The application client intercepts the token and routes users directly to their assigned layout dashboard.

Page 1.2: Password Reset Execution & Recovery Workflow
- Viewport Priority: Desktop and Mobile adaptive layout.
- UI Components:
  • Input Field: Registered Phone Number (Safaricom/Airtel) or Corporate Email.
  • CTA Button: Request Reset Code.
  • Secondary Component: 6-digit numeric verification box overlay (OTP Input Field).
- UI Workflow Actions:
  1. User states they forgot their password and submits their phone number.
  2. System fires a low-cost SMS API containing a time-bounded (5-minute expiry) numerical hash code.
  3. The UI automatically transitions into the OTP verification state. Upon correct numeric input entry, the layout exposes two hidden secure fields: New Password Input and Confirm Password Input, featuring an active client-side regex check for security validation.

2. Headteacher & Admin Dashboard Module
---------------------------------------

Page 2.1: Centralized Executive Overview (The Command Center)
- RBAC Scope: Accessible strictly by SuperAdmin, SchoolOwner, and Headteacher.
- UI Components:
  • KPI Scorecard Metrics (Grid View):
    - Total Active Pupils Count
    - Term-to-Date Fee Collection Realized (KES)
    - Outstanding Arrears Portfolio Value (KES)
    - Daily Staff/Student Attendance Index (%)
  • Data Visualization Widgets:
    - Line Chart tracking monthly fee collections against recurring operation bills.
    - Bar Chart highlighting average performance descriptors across different Grade Streams (Grade 1 through Grade 6).

Page 2.2: Multi-Tenant RBAC Settings & User Configuration
- RBAC Scope: Restricted to SuperAdmin and SystemAdministrator.
- UI Components:
  • Tabbed Navigation: Staff Profiles, Role Definition Matrices, and Permission Toggles.
  • The Matrix Component Table: A large cross-functional grid setting specific user types (Bursar, Teacher, ClassRepresentative) on the Y-Axis against database operation permissions (Create Invoices, Modify Grades, Wipe Records) on the X-Axis.

| ROLE MANAGEMENT ENGINE |
| System Role   | View Fin Ledgers | Edit Assessment | Export System |
| Headteacher   | [🟢 Enabled]     | [🟢 Enabled]    | [🟢 Enabled]  |
| Class Teacher | [🔴 Disabled]    | [🟢 Enabled]    | [🔴 Disabled] |
| School Bursar | [🟢 Enabled]     | [🔴 Disabled]   | [🟢 Enabled]  |

Page 2.3: Tenant Enrollment Control Panel (Admission Engine)
- UI Components:
  • Step-by-Step Multi-Stage Form Wizard:
    - Stage 1: Student Bio Data (Full Name, Date of Birth, Gender, Nemis/UPI Number identifier).
    - Stage 2: Academic Placement Selection (Drop-downs for Grade Level, Active Stream allocation).
    - Stage 3: Primary Guardian Relationship Mapping (Input fields for Parent Mobile, Secondary Phone, Work Email).
  • CTA Action Button: Register Student & Instantiate Financial Ledger.

3. Academic & CBC Management Module
-----------------------------------

Page 3.1: The Interactive Formative Assessment Matrix
- RBAC Scope: Editable by ClassTeacher and SubjectTeacher. View-only for Headteacher. Hidden from Bursar.
- UI Components:
  • Context-Filtering Ribbon: Selectors for Grade Class, Subject Block, and Target KICD Sub-Strand Node.
  • Horizontal Touch Table Grid: Leftmost column locks the student name and admission ID. The subsequent columns represent specific classroom evaluation parameters.
- UI Workflow Actions:
  1. Tapping an intersection cell pops open a bottom drawer tray on the viewport displaying 4 colored evaluation targets: EE, ME, AE, and BE.
  2. Selecting a metric updates the background color of the cell instantaneously using asynchronous JavaScript hooks, storing it directly into the IndexedDB caching instance to preserve data integrity during localized internet brownouts.

Page 3.2: Comprehensive KPSEA Report Compilation Desk
- UI Components:
  • Active Progress Tracking Indicator (Progress bar displaying completion status of terminal assessments across all subjects).
  • Data Validation Alert Matrix (Flags list of missing grading parameters or unchecked sub-strands).
  • Action CTA Button: Compile and Publish Digital Terminal Report Forms.
- UI Workflow Actions:
  1. Clicking compilation fires an analytical execution script compiling continuous assessment metrics across Grade 4, 5, and 6.
  2. Generates print-ready PDFs formatted precisely to match Ministry of Education regulatory guidelines, with a secondary button to push copies straight to the parent digital portal feed.

4. School Bursar & Financial Management Module
----------------------------------------------

Page 4.1: Live Ledger Oversight & M-Pesa Hook Activity Feed
- RBAC Scope: Write access for Bursar and SuperAdmin. Read-only access for Headteacher. Completely hidden from ClassTeacher.
- UI Components:
  • Dual Panel View layout.
  • Panel A (Left): Running stream of incoming real-time webhooks (displays M-Pesa transaction codes, timestamp strings, incoming currency values, and billing references).
  • Panel B (Right): Detailed ledger inspector interface showing items linked to selected accounts.
- UI Workflow Actions:
  1. When a transaction hits the system, it displays on the active layout panel with a pulse notification style.
  2. Unresolved or mistyped payment descriptors display an alert badge labeled Unallocated Transaction. Clicking it triggers a modal enabling manual mapping search bars to tie the funds to the correct admission file.

Page 4.2: Structured Fee Matrix Setup & Invoicing Suite
- UI Components:
  • Creation Input Form: Fee Component Title (e.g., Tuition, Transport Route A, Digital Content Access Fee).
  • Billing Cadence Selection (Dropdown toggling between Termly, Annually, or One-Off occurrences).
  • Target Cohort Allocation Toggles (Checkboxes to select matching student sets like Grade 4 or specific transport lines).
  • Primary CTA Button: Generate Termly Bulk Invoice Roll-out.

5. Parent Portal Module
-----------------------

Page 5.1: Multi-Pupil Ward Navigation Panel
- RBAC Scope: Restricted strictly to authenticated Guardian phone profiles.
- UI Components:
  • Card Layout Profiles: Renders discrete thumbnail profile images, current active classes, and financial states for each child registered under the parent's primary phone number interface.
  • Action UI Component: Clicking an individual student card dynamically shifts the master session parameters to load data specific to that student.

Page 5.2: Student Academic Timeline & Performance Index
- UI Components:
  • Accordion dropdown lists grouped dynamically by KICD Learning Areas.
  • Visual KPI Badges displaying descriptive summaries (Exceeding Expectations, etc.) with explanatory info tips to map technical educational markers into simple language layouts.
  • Download Component: Direct links to fetch compiled official signed PDF terminal grade documents.

Page 5.3: Integrated Micro-Billing & Payment Trigger Widget
- UI Components:
  • Financial Breakdown Card (Itemizes individual balances due across Tuition, Exams, and Meals).
  • Input Numeric Component: Payment Amount Field.
  • CTA Secondary Button: Initiate Immediate M-Pesa Payment.
- UI Workflow Actions:
  1. Parent edits the numerical value or keeps the full balance default.
  2. Clicking the payment asset activates an external API integration loop communicating with your payment gateway worker.
  3. Fires an STK PIN prompt directly onto the parent's mobile handset device, blocking the layout state using a modal spinner loading wheel animation until the webhook signals success.

6. Communication & System Broadcast Desk
----------------------------------------

Page 6.1: Dual-Channel Broadcast Messenger Hub
- RBAC Scope: Accessible by SuperAdmin, Headteacher, and Bursar.
- UI Components:
  • Audience Segment Filter Group (Multi-select boxes targeting All Parents, Grade 5 Parents, Transport Users Route B, or Staff Members).
  • Text Input Area featuring a hardcoded 160-character boundary indicator tracking line.
  • Routing Priority Checkbox options: Prefer Low-Cost WhatsApp Delivery Route or Enforce Direct Carrier SMS Delivery Line.
  • CTA Button: Dispatch Mass Communication Payload.

UI Architecture Summary
-----------------------
- Mobile-first responsive layout across all portals.
- JWT-based role routing after authentication.
- Multi-tenant sub-domain context for dynamic school branding.
- RBAC matrix: SuperAdmin / SchoolOwner / Headteacher / Bursar / ClassTeacher / SubjectTeacher / Guardian.
- CBC Formative Assessment Matrix with offline IndexedDB caching and color-coded EE/ME/AE/BE cells.
- M-Pesa STK push integration with modal spinner state management.
- 160-character SMS boundary indicator for broadcast messaging.
- Print-ready KPSEA PDF compilation aligned to Ministry of Education guidelines.